{"c":[{"id":"2bb07e0a9d672229","sum":"Skip test_coverage_collection to keep torch; its coverage-engine sync removes torch. Zstd: filter persistent or no .wal; replayed rows persistent=false Uncompressed; persistent segments ZSTD. Puck 09ea4ae: copy stayed v1.0.0+, no index; 1.5.4 wrote, 2.0.0 read; inode unchanged.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"04ad6c4e13eff575","sum":"Full pytest drops torch via test_coverage_collection make coverage-engine exact sync. Later: No module named torch.distributed; ensure-env, then rerun. Zstd check: filter persistent or no .wal. Replayed rows persistent=false Uncompressed; persistent segments are ZSTD.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261023T144151Z-19beeb928bb79a4a","text":"Measured 2026-10-23: a bare full pytest run in a torch-provisioned checkout drops torch midway: test_coverage_collection runs make coverage-engine, whose sync is exact. Later torch-gated tests fail (No module named torch.distributed); ensure-env, then rerun them.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261023T152930Z-94e11b6c634d81a7","text":"DuckDB 2.0.0, measured 2026-10-23: a zstd-column file opened read-only with a .wal (killed ingest) lists the replayed rows in pragma_storage_info as persistent=false, Uncompressed; every persistent segment is ZSTD. A zstd check must filter persistent or run with no .wal.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c67ab4511ba06727","sum":"pytest --ignore=tests/test_coverage_collection.py keeps torch; only that module make coverage-engine exact sync removes it. Puck step 8.4 at 09ea4ae exited 0 in 43s: shadow copy stayed v1.0.0+, schema head, no index. DuckDB 1.5.4 wrote it and 2.0.0 read it. Live inode unchanged.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261023T154646Z-7f876ab5674122fe","text":"QA 2026-10-23: in a torch-provisioned live checkout, pytest --ignore=tests/test_coverage_collection.py runs the rest of the suite and keeps torch; only that module's make coverage-engine runs the exact sync that removes it.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261023T164313Z-a987fa985b63d02d","text":"Puck step 8.4 at 09ea4ae exited 0 in 43s: shadow copy stayed v1.0.0+, schema head, no index. DuckDB 1.5.4 wrote it and 2.0.0 read it. Live warehouse inode unchanged.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"beb7790cb872e159","sum":"L4 PR tip drops memory-bank/active (Fresh; unmerged). Restore from main, rebase onto squash; merge rebase drops bank. Docs as-is; history separate/omitted; Make tables=indexes; STE100 steps. Arch: cutoffs+schema snapshot, not filenames or versions. Schema-docs: diagram sources.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"cb6ae39a5d37dae5","sum":"L4 release PR is a child whose tip drops memory-bank/active, so main stays a Fresh /niko checkout. Do not merge that child back. After land, restore memory-bank/active onto a branch from main. Rebase onto the squash. A merge-commit rebase ends on main and drops the memory bank.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261023T170937Z-2ed4854315f18992","text":"Operator 2026-10-23: a mid-L4 release PR is a child of the working branch whose tip drops memory-bank/active, so main stays a Fresh /niko checkout. Do not merge that child back; the deletion would remove the working memory bank.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261023T174008Z-2f2719b3d24475d2","text":"After PR 150 lands, restore memory-bank/active from constrain-size-as-best-we-can onto a branch from main. Rebase onto the squash conflicts; a merge-commit rebase ends on main and drops the memory bank.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"8afc0a8c1d95c4dc","sum":"Operator 2026-10-23: docs state the current system; history separate or omitted. Make tables are indexes. Procedures are numbered STE100 steps. Architecture states migration cutoffs and the schema snapshot, not filenames or schema versions. Schema-docs names diagram's sources.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261023T185340Z-f0241d50f37fdbf8","text":"Operator 2026-10-23: user-facing docs describe the system as it is. History gets its own section or is omitted. Make tables are indexes. Critical procedures are short numbered STE100 steps.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261023T192936Z-7fa70422db429591","text":"Operator 2026-10-23: architecture states migration cutoffs and the schema snapshot, not filenames or schema versions. Contributing schema-docs says the diagram is generated and which sources to edit.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
